<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump's world? Leaders navigate consequences of US policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b69afca54b328a03accfcc7a964a1da5b2921a24c3e458c4243ccd2f66e3caf9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T18:14:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy--bf2ad7c85eca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Donald Trump went to the rostrum of the United Nations General Assembly - and after taxing an axe to US aid and development funding, read the world the riot act. One Iran war later, the US president sticking to script with a speech that borrowed much of the language of last year. With citizens on five continents now feeling the pain at the pump, we'll ask what it will take to tame a global energy crisis whose potential spiral mirrors the contagion of hostilities from the Strait of Hormuz to the mouth of the Red Sea?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Watch live: French President Emmanuel Macron addresses UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a39ab564e9e7bd99d23f60c60528b96794a195c3e84d3699bcf0cf1d749daf9e</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:41:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, AI and the ICC: Trump makes threats, touts policies at UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4b3b64191511fa7bafae52455649f50f4c626d17e35e3ccff2050cf469e653</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly--12d297e3d635.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump launched a full-throated defence of the deeply unpopular US-Israeli war against Iran before the UN General Assembly on Tuesday, claiming that Washington would reach a deal with Tehran after the upcoming US midterm elections. Trump also rejected the idea of global regulation of artificial intelligence, said the government of Cuba would soon "fall", and urged member countries of the International Criminal Court to "resign".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: 'Nobody with a conscience can close their eyes to what is happening in Gaza', Erdogan tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1c5cb422dc09155d180db22ae82a82affb342b5b10702c57d06c9ed99608db</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:24:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6bc8aaa4cc3f94ffb9b70caf1c24a02a33ba9ce048fe86bc95ac7c391f02cfc</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms--aa11d208ea3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Trump defends Iran war, attacks ICC in UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fa3a434ceac78be77fb37eea0dbe3ae7c13b36445bd23cf8c343f79c98a6b6d</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:13:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-trump-defends-iran-war-attacks-icc-in-un-speech--62e72858513d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-trump-defends-iran-war-attacks-icc-in-un-speech" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump called Tuesday for all nations that are part of the International Criminal Court to quit the body, calling it "out of control." He also used the speech to argue that the war with Iran prevented Tehran from obtaining a nuclear weapon and warn that he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if no deal is reached to end the conflict. Watch his speech in full above.</summary></entry><entry><title>How is the EU responding to record fuel prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78eaef24a39b2a4f255c60c0ea34e1bd5af1bd1a72b19194d73fb0c853607e64</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices--5f583fca1c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">Fuel prices have hit record highs across Europe in recent days, driven by soaring oil prices amid the war in the Middle East and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries. However, the scale of the increases, as well as the measures taken to address them, varies significantly from one EU country to another. Here’s why.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Syrian man reunited with secret library hidden for 15 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12a9dbd64ba61c34e32dfe1f7dddc0e4df67d5aef4c917c49a281ecdeb160e74</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T15:15:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-syrian-man-reunited-with-secret-library-hidden-for-15-years--4bc11dedc9dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-syrian-man-reunited-with-secret-library-hidden-for-15-years" /><summary type="html">A Syrian man has been reunited with his collection of over 100 Islamic texts, science books and poems,15 years after sealing the collection behind a wall. Mustafa Khaled Alwan had built to conceal the library, which would likely have landed in prison, or worse, under Bashar al-Assad's rule.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lady Diana: Spencer’s memoir on Diana reignites royal controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac05a2599c24b10f7c090a2420ac5237c27724a4ddba6d82764c0f65961e4505</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:59:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-lady-diana-spencer-s-memoir-on-diana-reignites-royal-controversy--b74044b1ff2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-lady-diana-spencer-s-memoir-on-diana-reignites-royal-controversy" /><summary type="html">Prince Charles married with Lady Diana in 1981. The couple divorced in 1996 and a decade later Charles married Camilla Parker Bowles, now Queen Camilla. 
 
Spencer has long clashed with the royals over their treatment of his older sister.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN climate change body accused of conflict of interest, Saudi influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c80c6d97c862a3e95e915673377497ef0e90a5226ac49e1b98e847d9cc3119f9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:38:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-un-climate-change-body-accused-of-conflict-of-interest-saudi-influence--63663ec056ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-un-climate-change-body-accused-of-conflict-of-interest-saudi-influence" /><summary type="html">An investigation conducted by the Guardian is raising questions about potential conflicts of interest among experts helping produce the next major assessment from the UN’s Inter-governmental Panel on Climate Change. Out of the 223 lead authors in the part of the body which assesses how emissions can be reduced or removed, 20 have a strong conflict of interest, according to the investigation, with more than half linked to Saudi institutions, including two employees of oil giant Saudi Aramco.</summary></entry><entry><title>Guterres delivers 'message to superpowers' in last UN General Assembly speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1552c437a38128d597c6b96ef6c5b08a7412452c1169d14de293a1f0218d3b5c</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:28:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guterres-delivers-message-to-superpowers-in-last-un-general-assembly-speech--e5335de47362.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guterres-delivers-message-to-superpowers-in-last-un-general-assembly-speech" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres pleaded for “a world built on interdependence” as he made his final address Tuesday to the General Assembly, a yearly gathering of world leaders, in a message that was largely intended for the world's superpowers, says France 24's UN correspondent Jessica Le Masurier.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Trump set to defend Iran war in speech before UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68577248b12a12e83a34b7b30a451c9bd31003600939f22f53c7d0bfa0468146</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: UN chief Guterres makes final address to the General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d62700f831a015ba0f269c974ec1973dce5806ff47f179a657657140608590f0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:11:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-un-chief-guterres-makes-final-address-to-the-general-assembly--53ca6bc1fe8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-un-chief-guterres-makes-final-address-to-the-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">United Nations Secretary-General Antonio Guterres used ​his final address to the General Assembly on Tuesday to urge world leaders to regulate artificial intelligence, end wars, focus on climate change and overhaul UN institutions he warned are struggling to confront mounting global challenges. Watch his speech in full above.</summary></entry><entry><title>From slavery to today: The Black women who shaped America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed35649d175969c65049c36ab6863dc72f999b3860b837058edd16fc300b28c6</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:06:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260922-from-slavery-to-today-the-black-women-who-shaped-america--559ae654c697.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260922-from-slavery-to-today-the-black-women-who-shaped-america" /><summary type="html">"If you don’t understand the history of Black women, you don’t understand the history of America." Those words from Nobel Prize-winning novelist Toni Morrison open Sasha Bonét's debut memoir, "The Waterbearers". The New York writer traces three generations of Black women in her family: her grandmother Betty Jean, the daughter of formerly enslaved people in Louisiana who went on to raise eleven children; her mother Connie, who sought a middle-class life in majority-white Houston; and Sasha herself, now raising her daughter Sofia in New York.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Guatemala receives first US arms in nearly 50 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8159247a37cf42d251c9577107b8d744f6a315654bb3b0f23ded4f16c6ff5650</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:48:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:05:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guatemala-receives-first-us-arms-in-nearly-50-years--6670e6930b1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guatemala-receives-first-us-arms-in-nearly-50-years" /><summary type="html">Guatemala on Monday received the first batch of military weapons from the US in almost five decades. It ends an arms embargo implemented by the US due to human rights violations made during Guatemala's civil war. The US has continued to cooperate with Guatemala in recent years in the battle against drug trafficking.</summary></entry><entry><title>'UN unable to bring peace to conflicts: We haven’t seen this level of violence in decades’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3861f5ae53c9f392e396e5b98c7c155b56fb0d4f3d8ef0bf1e7058dbdfd303b</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:04:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades--6d0a22913e8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades" /><summary type="html">Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi is pleased to welcome Fanny Badache, Researcher at Sciences Po and Lecturer at the University of Geneva. The UN mandate is international peace and security, yet its ability to fulfill that mandate ultimately depends on the cooperation of sovereign states, namely the five powerful permanent members of the Security Council. As the UN is confronted with an increasingly fragmented, volatile and unpredictable international order, Badache argues that when those powers are divided, the mechanisms designed to enable collective security can instead produce paralysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US threatens South Sudan with sanctions over aid obstruction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3a7fe463b7679a5dc7ee0011ad48e3b40df6be57333f9dfdf5b3f2c505c163c</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:34:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-us-threatens-south-sudan-with-sanctions-over-aid-obstruction--7dafdfc0aa9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-us-threatens-south-sudan-with-sanctions-over-aid-obstruction" /><summary type="html">The United States has threatened to impose sanctions on South Sudan over alleged obstruction of humanitarian assistance, accusing officials at national, state and local levels of treating aid as a source of revenue.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ladin: Dolomites villages refuse to give up on ancient language</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b8558801d982ae9313cdb5b0b328e1337a46b9b223d7e6ed24e87d4f1aa0436</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:30:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language--e899b61b23c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language" /><summary type="html">Year after year, the mountains of the Dolomites become more popular with tourists. Amid millions of visitors, 30,000 inhabitants speak a language only they understand: Ladin, one of the oldest minority languages in Europe.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian armed groups announce anti-government alliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b53e40aba83ff472f6cee1bbb89871696cdf1c00c3d7736dcd6751c4a427576f</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:29:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-ethiopian-armed-groups-announce-anti-government-alliance--2435689d6502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-ethiopian-armed-groups-announce-anti-government-alliance" /><summary type="html">On the eve of International Peace Day, an Ethiopian rebel leader announced an alliance of seven armed groups with the stated objective of toppling Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's ruling party and establishing a transitional government. The alliance consists of former enemies during the 2020 civil war that killed 600,000 people, and other armed groups from across the country, all fighting their own battles against federal troops. With the war in Sudan across the border, and several third parties like Eritrea siding with involved parties, there are fears of isolated armed conflicts in Ethiopia spilling over into a regional war. More from our correspondent Tom Canetti.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nutrition expert shares easy steps to healthier eating</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec36cc114b8a7730336b5c081722277c7fd48d9f78a8c06633881ce99c6e4072</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260922-nutrition-expert-shares-easy-steps-to-healthier-eating--4a20e2c1b387.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260922-nutrition-expert-shares-easy-steps-to-healthier-eating" /><summary type="html">In this edition we're looking at how to eat healthier. We speak to Cynthia Ka, the author of "Mes assiettes naturo". Cynthia says cooking is your pharmacy and doing your weekly shopping is a powerful act. We find out what her go-to recipe is and how we can all make the change to healthier eating.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>New report tackles problem of governments' overreliance on consulting firms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc35445f4a75ca5f2b1aeacc0cc0144e3e1b7a006901530a502ef70b8d9efd67</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:35:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-new-report-tackles-problem-of-governments-overreliance-on-consulting-firms--d30a4173eb4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-new-report-tackles-problem-of-governments-overreliance-on-consulting-firms" /><summary type="html">Dependence on consulting firms is a growing trend among governments globally. Left unchecked, it can have a negative impact due to high costs or transparency issues. Such dependence came to the fore in France a few years ago, when the Macron government was criticised for its close ties with US consulting giant McKinsey. UNESCO's Inclusive Policy Lab, headed by Iulia Sevciuc, has established a new blueprint to tackle this problem. She spoke to us in Business.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>New book by Princess Diana's brother sparks royal ruckus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd712c0777dc528039bf79f72790c3e319143da1a4bbb708a46327eba33c32f</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:09:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-new-book-by-princess-diana-s-brother-sparks-royal-ruckus--ea6f053f6380.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-new-book-by-princess-diana-s-brother-sparks-royal-ruckus" /><summary type="html">A new book published Tuesday by the brother of the late Princess Diana has made headlines around the world with its damning allegations about Diana's ex-husband, now King Charles III, and reopened decades-old wounds within Britain's royal family. France 24's correspondent in London Benedicte Paviot has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron calls on EU to tackle soaring energy prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b72f637df8d6ec692e033f662475b4472d90d9dd360b724294551a04ae69dd9</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:08:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-macron-calls-on-eu-to-tackle-soaring-energy-prices--e1dc1ec20a1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-macron-calls-on-eu-to-tackle-soaring-energy-prices" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron has written to the EU Commission president, Ursula von der Leyen, calling on Brussels to take immediate action to lower energy prices. They have been on the rise as the conflict in the Middle East spreads, and as Ukraine's attacks on Russian diesel refineries continue.</summary></entry><entry><title>Media ban 'an escalation even for Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6054e4f66df931fc92258e8c8905b763bf7e57790cd056a0fdffe5e44b5ce4d</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:07:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-media-ban-an-escalation-even-for-trump--56a5dc4cba21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-media-ban-an-escalation-even-for-trump" /><summary type="html">CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Monday sued President Donald Trump’s administration days after they were barred from White House grounds, calling the selective ban — based on the content of their coverage — a “blatant violation” of the First Amendment. The extraordinary ban represents an escalation of Trump’s long-running efforts to restrict news coverage he finds objectionable, says France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani.</summary></entry></feed>
